our initial  shutdown was to prevent the overflow  of our hospitals and to allow us to meet  the demands caused by this global  pandemic  including the ventilators and a  permanent shutdown was  really never an option in terms of what  we're doing right now  this would be completely unsustainable  produce  debilitating economic fallback and lead  to catastrophic public health  consequences there are consequences to  shutdowns  that was president of course at his  coronavirus press briefing today fox  news medical correspondent mark segal is  on his way to washington tonight we're  sending him to the white house he's  going to interview the president  about what the administration is doing  to contain the wuhan coronavirus part 1  airs here at 8 pm eastern  part 2 on shannon's show at 11.  but first a new round of mandatory  shutdowns is pitting small business  owners  against their state governments the ones  they pay for  ian smith for example is the owner of  the attila's gym in belmar new jersey  we spoke to him earlier this year he  tried to open  his gym in defiance of a state shutdown  order  now he's taking extraordinary measures  to stay open he's even removed his front  door to prevent the state from keeping  the door closed too bad he's not an  abortion clinic or a liquor store he  would have no problem  at all ian smith joins us tonight ian  thanks so much for coming on  so thanks for having me state is trying  to shut you down  is there first to the science is there  evidence that your  gym has been a vector for a hotbed of  the spread of chronovirus  we have record of every single person  who has stepped foot  um and the total number of check-ins  well exceeding the thousands  uh not a single case has been reported  so far uh and we've kept detailed record  of that  uh all the way through okay so  i mean this literally you would have  been better off  joining a mob of rioters torching other  people's businesses  then you are responsibly following the  science and trying to keep belmar new  jersey healthy  why are you being hounded by the state  do you think  um i think that we are being haunted by  the state because  we are pushing back against a very very  clear political agenda at this point  and we've become a thorn in the side for  governor murphy  and my partner and i are not willing to  back down we're not going to have our  lives destroyed over a political agenda  that has nothing to do with us  so what is the governor threatening to  do to your gym  uh the police force was initially  weaponized against us with citation  after citation after citation uh then it  was the health department  uh we were shut down without anybody  ever stepping foot inside of our our  building  and then it's the court system the court  system enforced the shutdown  um and locked our doors on us and then  we finally got them removed and  we had workouts outside for a couple  weeks and the it was  it was absurd we were dragging half of  the gym outside close to 30 000 pounds  worth of equipment every single day  and on july 4th we resumed and now the  courts are being weaponized against us  again we were held in contempt of court  um and we we narrowly escaped that last  night  so again it's just a weaponization of  these public  organizations and offices that are meant  to serve and protect the people  and they're clearly being used to punish  us  yeah and a certain kind of people i mean  again if you're running a liquor store  selling state lotto tickets running an  abortion clinic you would have no  problem at all you  run a gym one of the healthiest  businesses by definition  this country has do you think it's odd  that they're  persecuting you i think it points to the  uh very clear fact that this is not  about public health  um first of all public health is not a  one-dimensional issue  public health does not start and finish  with covet there are many  other things that we have to consider  mental health being one of them  